From 20af55cfa34beefa3c10b7c5fe945b46a36544c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:09:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/40] lib/promscrape: acknowledge the rounds of targets
 exposing increments

A target exposing increments with client_golang's promhttp/delta commits
a round once its response is written, and written is not received: a
response in the socket's send buffer when the scrape timeout passes is
committed there and thrown away here, and the target's usage for that
scrape is lost. The target status page fetches a target's response to
show it, which for such a target took a round with it every time.

Such a target now names each round in X-Prometheus-Delta-Round, and holds
it until vmagent's next request says in X-Prometheus-Delta-Ack whether it
was processed; one that was not is reported again. vmagent sends "new"
before a target has named a round, then the last round processed in
full, a scrape processed in full being one that ends with up=1, or
"<session>:0" when none of a session was; the status page sends "peek",
which the target rolls back at once without touching the round the
scrape loop is on. ReadDeltaData carries the round of each request with
it, so a look at the status page never acknowledges what it fetched.
Other targets ignore the header; -promscrape.deltaAck=false turns it off.

End to end, the fork's sidecar and this vmagent, scraping every 2s with a
1s timeout, the sidecar stalling every third scrape past it after writing
the whole response and the status page opened five times: 3892 written,
3892 received, against 1266 (-67.5%) with -promscrape.deltaAck=false.
---
 lib/promscrape/client.go         |  43 +++++++++---
 lib/promscrape/delta_ack_test.go | 117 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 lib/promscrape/scraper.go        |   3 +
 lib/promscrape/scrapework.go     |  57 ++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 208 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 lib/promscrape/delta_ack_test.go

